; §18 stretch — arity-violation. The manifest declares `(double n)`
; with `:arity (fixed 1)`; the call below passes three positional
; arguments. The validator catches the mismatch *before* dispatch and
; surfaces `arity_mismatch` at the call site. The plugin's `double`
; export is never invoked — proves the arity gate sits ahead of the
; wasm runtime, not behind it. Skipped on Zig-native + TS-parity
; (no wasm runtime).
(use-plugin "double")

(double 1 2 3)
